Leo: Not yet. I''ve heard a robot has been built there that can talk.
Mia: Yes, it''s amazing. It answers your questions about space and stars.
Leo: That sounds great. What else can we see?
Mia: There''s a model of an electric car that has been designed by students.
Leo: Wow. I''d love to know how it works.
Mia: Then let''s go this Saturday. Tickets have already been booked for us.
Leo: Perfect. I can''t wait to learn something new!', '米娅问利奥去没去新科技馆;利奥没去,听说那里造了会说话的机器人;它能回答关于太空和星星的问题;还有学生设计的电动车模型;两人决定周六去,门票已经订好了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where are Mia and Leo talking about going?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The new science museum.","A football match.","A music concert.","A book shop."]},{"q":"What can the talking robot do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cook dinner for visitors.","Answer questions about space and stars.","Drive an electric car.","Sell tickets."]},{"q":"Who designed the electric car model?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Students.","Famous actors.","The museum cleaners.","Leo''s parents."]},{"q":"When will they go to the museum?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Next year.","This Saturday.","Tonight.","Never."]},{"q":"What has already been done for them?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Dinner has been cooked.","A car has been bought.","Tickets have been booked.","A robot has been sold."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
They are gunpowder, papermaking, printing and the compass.
Each of these inventions has changed the world in a deep way.
Thanks to the compass, sailors could travel far across the sea.
Even today, these old ideas are still used in modern life.', '古代中国以四大发明闻名:火药、造纸、印刷和指南针;每一项都深刻改变了世界;有了指南针,水手能远渡重洋;直到今天,这些古老的智慧仍用于现代生活。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How many great inventions is ancient China famous for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Two.","Ten.","None.","Four."]},{"q":"Which of these is one of the four inventions?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The compass.","The television.","The aeroplane.","The computer."]},{"q":"What did each invention do to the world?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Made it smaller.","Changed it deeply.","Left it the same.","Destroyed it."]},{"q":"How did the compass help sailors?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They could fly to the Moon.","They could stop the wind.","They could travel far across the sea.","They could speak new languages."]},{"q":"Are these old ideas still useful today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["No, they are forgotten.","Only in museums.","Only in books.","Yes, they are still used."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Ben: Good idea. You ask the questions, and I''ll be the expert.
Anna: So, who was the telephone invented by?
Ben: It was invented by Alexander Graham Bell in 1876.
Anna: What gave him the idea?
Ben: His mother could not hear well, so he became interested in sound.
Anna: And what was the first phone call about?
Ben: He simply called his helper in the next room to test the machine.', '安娜和本排练关于电话发明的对话;安娜提问,本扮专家;电话由亚历山大·格雷厄姆·贝尔于1876年发明;因母亲听力不好,他对声音产生兴趣;第一通电话只是叫隔壁房间的助手来测试机器。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are Anna and Ben practising?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A conversation about the telephone''s invention.","A song about the sea.","A play about a king.","A maths lesson."]},{"q":"Who was the telephone invented by?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Benjamin Franklin.","Alexander Graham Bell.","Charles Darwin.","Isaac Newton."]},{"q":"In which year was it invented?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["1752.","1920.","1876.","2005."]},{"q":"Why did Bell become interested in sound?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He loved loud music.","He worked on ships.","He sold radios.","His mother could not hear well."]},{"q":"What was the first phone call about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Testing the machine with his helper.","Ordering a new kite.","Calling a doctor.","Buying a car."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
These machines can now make parts of the human body.
A patient once received a new ear that had been printed in a lab.
Because each part is made to fit one person, operations become safer.
In the future, fewer sick people may have to wait for help.', '科学家为3D打印机找到惊人新用途:这些机器如今能制造人体部件;曾有病人获得一只在实验室打印出的新耳朵;由于每个部件都为一个人量身打印,手术更安全;未来,需要等待救治的病人也许会更少。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What new use have scientists found for 3D printers?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Printing newspapers.","Making parts of the human body.","Building cars.","Cooking food."]},{"q":"What did one patient receive?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A new car.","A gold medal.","A printed ear.","A pet turtle."]},{"q":"Why are these operations safer?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The parts are very cheap.","The parts are very large.","The parts are made of paper.","Each part fits one person exactly."]},{"q":"What may happen in the future?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Fewer patients may have to wait.","Printers will disappear.","Doctors will stop working.","Bodies will stop growing."]},{"q":"Where was the new part printed?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["In a kitchen.","In a lab.","On a ship.","In a garden."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Grace: I think I''d like to be an astronomer and study the stars.
Teacher: That''s wonderful. And what about you, Sam?
Sam: I''m more interested in living things, so maybe a biologist.
Teacher: Both are excellent choices. Science needs curious minds.
Grace: But the maths looks really hard.
Teacher: Don''t worry. With patience, every difficult subject can be learned.
Sam: Then we''ll both keep trying!', '老师问格蕾丝想当哪种科学家;格蕾丝想当天文学家研究星星;山姆对生物更感兴趣,想当生物学家;老师说两者都很好,科学需要好奇心;格蕾丝担心数学太难;老师鼓励说只要有耐心,再难的科目也能学会;两人决定继续努力。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Grace want to be?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A biologist.","A driver.","An astronomer.","A singer."]},{"q":"What is Sam more interested in?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The stars.","Old cars.","Cooking.","Living things."]},{"q":"What does the teacher say science needs?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Curious minds.","A lot of money.","Big machines only.","Quiet students."]},{"q":"What is Grace worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The stars are far.","The maths is hard.","The class is boring.","The room is cold."]},{"q":"What does the teacher say about difficult subjects?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They should be avoided.","They are useless.","They can be learned with patience.","They never change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Most new ideas begin with a problem that needs a solution.
When something annoys us, we start to ask how it could be better.
That small question is often the first step of a great invention.
So never stop being curious, because every question may change the world.', '关于发明有个简单的道理:大多数新点子始于一个需要解决的问题;当某件事让我们烦恼时,我们便开始思考如何让它变得更好;那个小小的问题,往往是伟大发明的第一步;所以永远别停止好奇,因为每个问题都可能改变世界。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where do most new ideas begin?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["With a lot of money.","With a famous name.","With a big factory.","With a problem that needs solving."]},{"q":"What do we do when something annoys us?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["We ask how it could be better.","We forget about it.","We go to sleep.","We sell it."]},{"q":"What is often the first step of a great invention?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A long holiday.","A small question.","A new car.","A loud noise."]},{"q":"What should we never stop being?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Angry.","Tired.","Curious.","Silent."]},{"q":"Why is curiosity important?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It makes us rich.","It saves time.","It ends all problems.","Every question may change the world."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3', 'fltrp');

